{
  "manufacturer": "Siemens",
  "manufacturer_slug": "siemens",
  "model": "SINAMICS V20 inverter (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "sinamics-v20",
  "short_model": "SINAMICS V20",
  "aliases": [
    "V20",
    "6SL3210-5BB",
    "6SL3210-5BE"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "SINAMICS V20 basic inverters (1AC 230 V 6SL3210-5BB.. and 3AC 400 V 6SL3210-5BE..) using the built-in RS485 port with P2023 = 2 (Modbus), per operating instructions A5E34559884-006 (11/2016).",
  "summary": "Siemens' compact general-purpose inverter, with an RS485 port on the control terminals that runs USS by default and Modbus RTU when P2023 = 2. The drive exposes two holding-register blocks: a MICROMASTER-style block from 40001 with individual run/fault/direction bits and scaled measurements, and a block from 40100 with the raw control word, setpoint, status word and actual value plus scaled measurements, fault history and PID settings. This map covers both blocks except the generic parameter-access window.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The mapping table prints each register twice: an 'Inverter' number starting at 0 and a 'MODBUS' number starting at 40001 (e.g. 0 = 40001, 99 = 40100). The inverter number is the value that goes into the request, so subtract 40001 from the Modicon number: control word 40100 is wire address 99."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "SINAMICS V20 Inverter Operating Instructions",
    "doc_number": "A5E34559884-006",
    "revision_date": "2016-11",
    "url": "https://cache.industry.siemens.com/dl/files/991/109743991/att_906061/v1/V20_op_instr_1116_en-US.pdf",
    "pages": "Section 7.2 MODBUS communication pp. 170-178 (function codes p. 170-171, exception codes and basic settings pp. 172-173, mapping table pp. 174-177, scaling/BICO/F72 pp. 177-178); macro Cn011 p. 73; RS485 termination p. 165; parameter list r0052 p. 190, r0054 p. 191, P2010/P2014 p. 268, r2018 pp. 269-270, P2019 pp. 271-272, P2021-P2023 p. 273"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All values are single 16-bit registers; there are no 32-bit values in the map. Scaled values are sent as the engineering value multiplied by the table's scaling factor (e.g. 100 for 0.01 resolution), so the scale here is 1 / factor.",
    "Signed/unsigned is not printed per register; registers with a negative range in the table are INT16, the rest UINT16. Ramp times and P2000 reach raw values above 32767 (650.0 s x 100, 550.00 Hz x 100), which only fits as unsigned.",
    "Left out: 40002 Watchdog action (the manual gives no action codes), 40035 Stop/run (its on/off text order contradicts the status bit it mirrors), 40349 Hand/auto (r0807 only reports whether an external client has master control; the HAND/AUTO text is not tied to a bit value), 40013 (reserved), and the parameter-access window 40550-40559 (parameter number, index, upper/lower word) because the access procedure is not described.",
    "40003 and 40044 are the setpoint and actual value in % (factor 100); 40101 and 40111 are the same process data unscaled, where 4000 hex = 100 % of P2000.",
    "Writing a BICO register (e.g. 40014/40200 digital output, 40009/40500 PID enable) fixes that BICO input to a static 0 or 1 and drops its previous connection; reading returns the BICO output.",
    "This is the 11/2016 edition; a newer 05/2022 edition exists on the Siemens support site but its direct PDF link refused automated download, so it was not used."
  ],
